 ],
 "description": "Rules: each case's `short` is expanded with the defaults, or with `options` when given, and each record in `records` is checked against the result. `failures` lists the rule failures the check reports, in order, each with `pointer`, the JSON pointer of the object the rule sits on (\"\" for the root, /approvals/1 for a rule on the items of approvals), and `message`. It lists nothing for the type's own keywords: a record that also breaks those, such as a date field holding something that isn't a date, lists only its rule failures. Failures are ordered by pointer, in document order (an object before the objects inside it), then by the order of the rules on one object. Among sibling members of one object, the order is property name order, by code point; among a list's items, it is index order. `unique` and `within` fail once for each offending value, in the order the values first appear; every other rule fails at most once per object."
}
